2026-07-29 09:16:32,591 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What fields should be included in the eCRF?", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 73, "section": "11.3 Confidentiality of Patient Data"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 58, "section": "8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.1 Recruitment"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 38, "section": "4.4 Withdrawal Criteria"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 80, "section": "16.1 Investigator File"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 37, "section": "4.3.1 Prior and Concomitant Therapies"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 70, "section": "Trial-specific Source Data Requirements"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 75, "section": "12.2 Deviations from the Protocol"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 52, "section": "6.4 Unscheduled Visits"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 78, "section": "14.5 Patient Information and Consent"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 76, "section": "13.1 Clinical Trial Report"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 64, "section": "Expedited Reporting by the Sponsor or CRO"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 29, "section": "3.3 Safety Review Committee"}], "context_char_count": 17302, "response": "## Fields to be Included in the eCRF\n\nBased on the protocol, the following fields and data elements should be captured in the electronic Case Record Form (eCRF):\n\n### 1. Patient Identification & Screening\n- Unique screening number (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 36)\n- Reason for screening failure, if the patient is not randomised (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 36)\n\n### 2. Adverse Event Log\nEach adverse event entry must include (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 58):\n- Adverse event description\n- Date of onset (time, if applicable)\n- Intensity\n- Causal relationship to IMP\n- Action taken to IMP\n- Other action taken\n- Date and time of outcome\n- Outcome\n- Seriousness\n\n### 3. Serious Adverse Events (SAEs)\n- Demographics (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 63)\n- Adverse Event Log (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 63)\n- Medical History Log (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 63)\n- Concomitant Medication Log (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 63)\n\n### 4. Concomitant Medications & Prior Therapies\n- Details of all concomitant medications, including the main reason for prescription (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 37)\n- Prior treatment for UC within 12 months of Visit 1 (Screening) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 37)\n\n### 5. Withdrawal / Discontinuation\n- Date of premature termination (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 38)\n- Main reason for discontinuation (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 38)\n- If discontinuation is due to an adverse event, the specific event must be recorded (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 38)\n- Patient must be registered as discontinued in the eCRF (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 38)\n\n### 6. Unscheduled Visits\n- Description of the visit including the reason for the visit (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 52)\n\n### 7. Protocol Deviations\n- Documentation of any deviations, including description, relevant dates (start and stop), and action taken (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 75)\n\n### 8. Source Data / Patient Records\nThe following minimum data points from hospital/medical source records must also be captured in the eCRF (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 70):\n- Documentation of signed and dated Informed Consent\n- Patient's name and date of birth\n- Screening/randomisation number\n- Body weight and height\n- Dosing of IMP \u2013 date of first and last dose\n- Occurrence of any adverse events/SAEs (including description and duration)\n- Medical history\n- Date of UC diagnosis\n- Date of each visit\n- Any assessment performed\n- Any concomitant therapy\n- Status of the patient at the end of trial\n\n> **Note:** All eCRF entries must be approved/authorised by the Investigator with an electronic signature. Errors are corrected electronically with automatic audit trail tracking, including the date, time, and name of the person making the correction (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 71).", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 428.42398291015644, 554.4000000000001, 387.7749752178487], [71.99999999999994, 183.1439829101563, 551.0399999999998, 142.4949752178486], [71.99999999999994, 711.8639829101563, 550.92, 671.2149752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 135.8639829101562, 541.0800000000002, 110.45497521784853], [72.0, 369.2639829101563, 555.6, 267.89497521784847]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 73, "section": "11.3 Confidentiality of Patient Data", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.0, 174.5039829101563, 549.8400000000001, 118.73497521784861], [71.99999999999983, 421.46398291015635, 540.8399999999997, 380.8149752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 58, "sec